Patch 2042: 4096 draw records per frame instead of 2048.

A J-Stars fight frame records more than 2048 draws, so nearly every fight frame was split by patch 2002's mid-frame flush
([MIDFLUSH] records=2040: about 5,000 in a 9-minute demo run), each split costing an extra render pass. With GPU vertex
pulling on (VPULL=1, patch 2034), draws are not merged at all and every frame was split: that is what froze the picture
in the earlier VPULL tests. The upload heaps grow with it (per-draw constants about 69 MB instead of 35).

Tested (US disc, attract demo, FRAME_TL=1): mid-frame flushes from about 5,000 to 40 per run; the drain's time per demo
fight frame from 34-46 ms to 28-31 ms. The game still waits for a third vblank, so flips/s are about the same alone
(18.5 vs 17.3-18.5). With VPULL=1 the picture no longer freezes: drain 22-26 ms, 17.3-19.9 flips/s in four runs; VPULL
stays opt-in until that is measured more.

